Copyright and attribution
=========================

deconrnaseq-py is a Python re-implementation of the Bioconductor R package
**DeconRNASeq**, version 1.50.0 (Bioconductor 3.21, git commit 20915cd).

Original R package authors
--------------------------
* Ting Gong <tinggong@gmail.com>
* Joseph D. Szustakowski <joseph.szustakowski@novartis.com>

Original source: https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.21/bioc/src/contrib/DeconRNASeq_1.50.0.tar.gz
Original licence: GPL-2 (see the DESCRIPTION file of the R package).

Port
----
The Python port (this repository) is a derivative work of the R package and
is therefore distributed under the same licence: **GNU General Public
License, version 2** (see LICENSE for the full text).

The numerical algorithm — constrained least squares with a sum-to-one
equality and non-negativity constraints, optionally on R-`scale()`d data —
follows the R implementation `R/DeconRNASeq.R` of DeconRNASeq 1.50.0.
